[[0.0, 1.683, "The highest mountains on Earth"], [1.916, 2.833, "The Andes"], [6.283, 8.9, "Above the clouds, there was an empire"], [11.1, 12.4, "It stretched 4,000 km"], [12.6, 14.116, "from Seoul all the way to Vietnam"], [14.15, 14.833, "that's the distance"], [17.033, 18.4, "About 10 million people lived there"], [20.633, 21.766, "At the time, in the Americas"], [21.766, 22.916, "it was the largest nation"], [24.766, 26.416, "But this vast empire"], [26.5, 27.966, "had no writing"], [29.133, 31.1, "Egypt, Rome"], [31.633, 32.183, "and China too"], [32.25, 33.733, "Every great civilization"], [33.816, 34.616, "always had writing"], [35.833, 37.716, "But only the Inca had none"], [37.816, 39.0, "They had no money either"], [39.2, 40.4, "No wheeled carts"], [41.066, 41.566, "no iron"], [41.966, 43.183, "not a single one"], [43.7, 45.466, "With no writing, no money, no iron"], [45.7, 46.283, "how did they"], [46.35, 48.533, "rule such a vast empire?"], [49.366, 50.266, "Its name was the Inca"], [50.6, 51.666, "In just 100 years, it became"], [51.75, 52.733, "the strongest empire in the Americas"], [53.066, 55.0, "And to just 168 men"], [55.116, 56.716, "it fell in a single day"], [56.716, 59.3, "Now, the empire built above the clouds —"], [59.366, 60.7, "the story of the Inca begins"], [61.666, 62.0, "First"], [62.0, 63.85, "just how incredible this empire was"], [64.333, 65.6, "At 2,400 meters above sea level"], [65.68299999999999, 66.4, "where the clouds"], [66.4, 67.9, "lie below your feet, on the peaks"], [68.233, 70.25, "the Inca built cities from stone alone"], [70.633, 72.633, "Their stone walls are so precise"], [73.066, 74.95, "that between the stones, not a sheet of paper"], [75.066, 76.2, "not even a knife blade can fit"], [76.76599999999999, 77.71600000000001, "With no cement"], [77.883, 79.0, "and no iron tools"], [79.233, 80.416, "500 years have passed"], [80.7, 81.2, "In that time"], [81.2, 82.05, "powerful earthquakes"], [82.116, 83.65, "shook the Andes many times"], [84.333, 85.75, "The buildings the Spanish built on top"], [85.916, 87.233, "collapsed"], [87.96600000000001, 89.15, "But the walls the Inca built"], [89.233, 90.4, "still stand today"], [90.4, 91.366, "exactly as they were"], [91.96600000000001, 93.43299999999999, "Isn't that strange?"], [93.93299999999999, 95.55, "People with no iron, no wheels"], [95.616, 97.5, "and no writing"], [97.55, 98.7, "built earthquake-proof cities"], [98.75, 99.46600000000001, "above"], [99.46600000000001, 100.0, "the clouds"], [100.46600000000001, 101.88300000000001, "But the truly strange part"], [102.01599999999999, 102.816, "is something else"], [102.88300000000001, 105.01599999999999, "Most of the world's great civilizations"], [105.083, 106.68299999999999, "were born beside great rivers"], [108.43299999999999, 109.533, "Egypt, the Nile"], [110.533, 112.333, "Mesopotamia, between two rivers"], [113.46600000000001, 114.51599999999999, "China, the Yellow River"], [115.96600000000001, 118.1, "all wide, fertile plains"], [119.93299999999999, 122.016, "But the Inca were the opposite"], [123.85, 125.25, "On the highest"], [125.366, 127.033, "and harshest peaks in the world"], [128.233, 130.283, "that's exactly where they built their empire"], [131.133, 132.516, "And that's not the only difference"], [132.86599999999999, 134.016, "Egypt, Rome"], [134.15, 135.45, "and China all had writing"], [135.966, 137.266, "They had money and markets too"], [137.566, 139.333, "Even the Aztecs, from our last video"], [139.6, 140.11599999999999, "in huge"], [140.166, 141.516, "markets, used cacao"], [141.516, 142.833, "to buy and sell goods"], [143.5, 144.6, "But the Inca"], [145.03300000000002, 145.7, "had almost no writing"], [145.7, 147.5, "no money, and almost no markets"], [148.95, 150.266, "With no writing and no money"], [152.4, 153.916, "on the harshest land in the world"], [154.083, 155.7, "a nation built an empire of 10 million"], [156.7, 158.566, "In all of human history, a civilization like this"], [159.233, 160.816, "the Inca is almost the only one"], [161.966, 163.53300000000002, "How was it even possible?"], [164.3, 166.05, "The secret was three things"], [168.066, 169.1, "The Inca weren't"], [169.15, 170.266, "huge from the start"], [172.3, 173.083, "In the 13th century"], [174.03300000000002, 175.383, "in a small Andes valley"], [175.5, 176.383, "called Cusco"], [176.5, 177.9, "there was just one ordinary tribe"], [180.8, 182.733, "just one of hundreds of tribes"], [186.633, 188.333, "Then one king appeared"], [191.533, 192.86599999999999, "His name was Pachacuti"], [193.933, 195.216, "The meaning of his name is chilling"], [196.3, 197.566, "\"He who overturns the world\""], [198.6, 200.516, "And he truly overturned the world"], [201.933, 203.583, "Taking in neighbor after neighbor"], [203.666, 204.916, "in just 100 years"], [205.03300000000002, 206.55, "the small valley tribe"], [206.666, 208.55, "became an empire ruling all the Andes"], [210.133, 211.3, "The Inca called their nation"], [211.35, 213.016, "Tawantinsuyu"], [214.266, 215.6, "\"The Four Lands United\""], [216.03300000000002, 216.966, "At its very center"], [217.133, 218.61599999999999, "where all roads began"], [218.733, 219.53300000000002, "stood one single person"], [219.566, 220.416, "the emperor"], [221.7, 222.2, "This one single person"], [222.25, 223.316, "will become"], [223.36599999999999, 224.483, "very important later"], [225.7, 226.5, "Keep that in mind"], [228.0, 229.433, "The Inca had no money"], [230.566, 231.883, "No coins, no bills"], [231.966, 233.36599999999999, "and almost no markets"], [234.566, 236.36599999999999, "So how did they pay taxes?"], [238.36599999999999, 239.416, "The answer is surprising"], [239.53300000000002, 239.966, "The Inca people"], [239.966, 241.566, "paid their taxes not with money"], [241.683, 242.566, "but with labor"], [243.3, 244.316, "It was called the mita"], [245.033, 247.133, "The state gave land, gave food"], [247.216, 248.016, "and gave a home"], [248.8, 250.633, "In return, each year the people worked"], [250.8, 252.55, "a set number of days for the state"], [253.166, 254.05, "They built roads"], [254.133, 256.3, "made fields, and raised temples"], [256.33299999999997, 257.733, "Simply put, it was like this:"], [258.2, 259.183, "\"We won't take your money"], [259.216, 261.3, "just come work with us for a few days\""], [262.366, 263.866, "With this labor tax"], [264.166, 266.6, "the Inca built their 40,000 km of roads"], [267.1, 268.616, "and cities above the clouds"], [269.366, 271.033, "A nation where not a single coin circulated"], [272.483, 274.33299999999997, "pulled off one of the largest construction"], [274.45, 275.45, "projects in human history"], [276.266, 277.133, "The second secret"], [277.56600000000003, 278.85, "This one is the most amazing"], [281.83299999999997, 283.65, "To rule a nation of 10 million"], [283.683, 284.65, "you need records"], [286.166, 287.08299999999997, "How much tax"], [287.5, 288.25, "how many people"], [288.7, 290.0, "how much grain in the storehouse"], [292.766, 293.883, "But the Inca"], [293.966, 294.933, "had no writing"], [297.8, 299.383, "So instead of writing, the Inca"], [299.466, 300.5, "used knots"], [303.733, 305.566, "By tying knots on colored cords"], [305.7, 307.033, "they recorded information"], [307.633, 308.583, "It was called the quipu"], [308.933, 309.7, "The color of the cord"], [309.833, 310.733, "the shape of the knot"], [310.866, 312.066, "the position of the knot"], [312.433, 313.133, "with these three things"], [313.183, 314.7, "they recorded numbers and information"], [315.1, 315.833, "Simply put"], [315.833, 317.0, "it was an Excel file"], [317.08299999999997, 318.1, "written in knots"], [318.6, 319.416, "Across the country"], [319.5, 319.983, "there were officials"], [319.983, 321.816, "trained to read these knots"], [322.733, 324.3, "Just by touching the knots"], [324.35, 324.666, "they could tell which village"], [324.666, 326.35, "had how much grain"], [326.416, 327.7, "reading it off with ease"], [330.033, 330.866, "And here"], [331.066, 332.783, "is one chilling fact"], [333.3, 335.216, "Quipus that recorded numbers, today"], [335.283, 336.683, "scholars can mostly"], [336.85, 337.7, "read them"], [338.33299999999997, 339.733, "But some quipus, it is said"], [339.85, 340.65, "hold not numbers"], [340.883, 341.683, "but stories"], [341.81600000000003, 344.33299999999997, "and history"], [345.283, 346.733, "And those quipus"], [346.85, 349.05, "even now, 500 years later, no one"], [349.33299999999997, 350.883, "can fully read them"], [353.866, 356.3, "Knots holding the Inca's true history"], [356.766, 358.35, "may still be"], [358.5, 359.5, "somewhere in a museum"], [359.5, 360.5, "waiting to be"], [360.5, 362.0, "unraveled"], [365.2, 367.133, "The third secret: the roads"], [368.966, 370.483, "Across the entire Andes, the Inca"], [370.716, 372.8, "laid 40,000 kilometers of roads"], [373.933, 376.33299999999997, "That's the distance all the way around the Earth"], [376.7, 378.966, "With no iron tools and no wheels"], [379.9, 381.83299999999997, "But with no writing"], [381.983, 383.95, "how did they send orders far away?"], [385.166, 387.2, "The answer: people ran"], [388.4, 390.516, "Every few kilometers along the road"], [391.1, 392.6, "a runner stood waiting"], [393.366, 394.5, "They were called chasqui"], [395.33299999999997, 396.466, "One would run"], [396.5, 397.1, "with all his might"], [397.1, 398.983, "and pass the message to the next"], [400.4, 402.216, "Then that one would run again"], [402.933, 405.5, "Yes, it was literally a relay-race"], [405.65, 406.45, "delivery system"], [408.533, 410.56600000000003, "Thanks to the chasqui, something"], [410.716, 411.716, "unbelievable happened"], [415.733, 417.75, "Fresh fish caught"], [417.81600000000003, 418.366, "on the Pacific coast"], [420.3, 422.433, "reached the emperor's table above the clouds"], [422.633, 424.483, "in just two days"], [425.633, 426.566, "Hundreds of kilometers"], [426.816, 429.266, "across the rugged Andes mountains"], [430.566, 432.983, "The roads were the empire's veins"], [433.066, 433.916, "and its nerves"], [434.983, 436.45, "Orders, armies"], [436.533, 438.183, "and even fish flowed along these roads"], [438.3, 440.45, "to every corner of the empire"], [443.566, 445.916, "But the truly amazing thing about the Inca"], [446.266, 448.15, "is not the roads, nor the knots"], [450.533, 452.25, "Along the roads, the Inca built"], [452.25, 454.383, "huge stone storehouses"], [456.933, 458.1, "They were called qollqa"], [460.9, 463.033, "Inside, grain and cloth"], [463.15, 464.116, "were piled up"], [464.233, 465.033, "like mountains"], [470.933, 472.516, "In normal times, they went untouched"], [473.6, 475.31600000000003, "So when were they used?"], [477.233, 478.3, "When a drought came"], [478.9, 480.066, "or the harvest failed"], [480.15, 482.116, "the state opened these storehouses"], [483.033, 485.05, "and fed the people"], [486.533, 487.95, "Those too old to work"], [488.733, 489.583, "the sick"], [490.266, 491.45, "those who had lost a husband"], [492.966, 494.75, "In the Inca, even these people"], [495.1, 497.383, "were cared for by the state to the very end"], [499.4, 500.2, "Think about it"], [500.2, 502.366, "This was 500 years ago"], [504.2, 505.85, "In Europe, when harvests failed"], [506.016, 506.933, "countless people"], [507.1, 509.366, "starved to death in the streets"], [511.1, 511.716, "Above the clouds"], [511.716, 513.833, "in this empire, almost no one"], [514.316, 515.183, "starved to death"], [517.033, 518.65, "What held the Inca together"], [518.8, 520.716, "was not the sword, nor fear"], [522.466, 523.516, "\"We will let"], [523.633, 524.7, "no one go hungry\""], [525.5, 526.9159999999999, "It was this promise"], [528.066, 530.1, "Please remember this promise"], [530.583, 531.7, "At the end of the story"], [531.85, 533.133, "we will meet it again"], [535.833, 537.3, "The people of such a nation"], [537.55, 539.383, "achieved something truly remarkable"], [540.666, 541.65, "On the steep Andes"], [541.733, 543.533, "they carved the slopes into steps"], [543.733, 545.933, "and made huge terraced farms"], [547.9, 549.3, "They built stone terraces"], [550.133, 551.25, "filled them with soil"], [552.766, 554.033, "and ran water channels"], [555.466, 556.383, "Above the clouds"], [556.516, 558.033, "they farmed"], [559.3, 561.55, "High mountains freeze at night"], [562.933, 565.433, "The Inca turned this to their advantage"], [567.0, 568.916, "They froze potatoes overnight, then by day"], [569.15, 571.833, "pressed out the water and froze them again"], [573.033, 574.633, "This made chuño"], [575.433, 577.983, "the world's first freeze-dried food"], [578.15, 578.95, "that wouldn't rot"], [579.183, 579.966, "for years"], [580.433, 581.733, "The freeze-dried food"], [582.133, 582.933, "that astronauts eat —"], [582.966, 585.133, "the Inca were already making it"], [585.333, 586.933, "500 years ago"], [587.866, 590.016, "And at its peak stood the city"], [590.133, 592.183, "above the clouds: Machu Picchu"], [593.6, 595.466, "Scholars believe it was the royal"], [595.616, 597.15, "retreat of the great king"], [597.3, 599.016, "Pachacuti"], [600.2, 601.766, "With no iron and no wheels"], [602.0, 604.366, "humans, with only their hands and stone"], [604.6, 606.0, "built a paradise above the clouds"], [607.866, 608.9, "Around the year 1500"], [609.016, 610.983, "the Inca stood at their peak"], [611.9, 613.933, "Everything seemed perfect"], [614.933, 616.05, "But at that very moment"], [616.25, 617.416, "an invisible enemy"], [617.566, 618.816, "was already approaching"], [618.933, 620.25, "from the north"], [623.333, 625.5, "Years before the Spanish army"], [625.616, 626.616, "ever reached the Inca"], [626.75, 627.55, "from the north"], [627.866, 630.266, "a strange disease began to spread"], [632.233, 633.816, "It was smallpox"], [633.816, 636.283, "a disease brought by the Europeans"], [637.55, 639.383, "Here you might wonder"], [641.333, 643.216, "The Europeans hadn't even arrived yet"], [643.65, 646.016, "so how did their disease come first?"], [646.733, 648.05, "Here's the secret"], [648.25, 649.116, "The Spanish had already"], [649.25, 650.766, "set foot in Central America"], [650.883, 652.05, "far to the north"], [652.25, 653.65, "of the Inca"], [654.65, 656.05, "The disease that began there"], [656.366, 657.1659999999999, "spread from person"], [657.25, 657.933, "to person"], [657.933, 659.216, "village to village"], [659.283, 660.816, "faster than the conquerors"], [660.933, 662.766, "racing down the continent"], [668.066, 668.883, "And here"], [669.016, 671.133, "a heartbreaking irony unfolds"], [671.633, 673.366, "The fast roads"], [673.483, 674.533, "that were the Inca's pride"], [674.733, 677.416, "instead carried the disease"], [677.616, 678.366, "to every corner of the empire"], [679.133, 680.816, "The roads that united the nation"], [680.983, 681.533, "became the roads"], [681.533, 683.3, "that destroyed it"], [683.533, 685.05, "The Inca people had"], [685.3, 687.05, "no immunity to this disease at all"], [688.166, 690.033, "Whole villages emptied"], [690.183, 691.116, "Scholars believe that"], [691.266, 692.583, "nearly half the Inca population"], [692.75, 694.866, "was lost at this time"], [695.6, 697.816, "And the most fatal death of all"], [698.016, 698.85, "the great emperor"], [699.216, 700.15, "Huayna Capac"], [700.366, 702.05, "fell to this disease"], [702.65, 703.683, "The problem was"], [703.766, 705.616, "he died suddenly"], [705.816, 708.216, "without naming a successor"], [708.6659999999999, 709.533, "Do you remember?"], [709.566, 711.816, "In the Inca, everything began"], [712.05, 713.733, "from one single person"], [713.816, 714.45, "the emperor"], [715.2, 716.5, "That one single person"], [716.633, 718.583, "vanished with no heir"], [719.3, 719.883, "The empire"], [719.9159999999999, 721.2, "even before the Spanish arrived"], [721.6, 723.283, "had already lost its head"], [724.266, 725.366, "With the emperor gone"], [725.483, 726.25, "two sons"], [726.25, 728.166, "clashed over the empty throne"], [729.033, 730.183, "The elder, Huascar"], [730.35, 732.15, "and the younger, Atahualpa"], [732.866, 734.933, "The war between the brothers was terrible"], [735.566, 737.183, "People of the same nation"], [737.3, 738.9, "killed each other for years"], [739.8, 741.5, "After a long civil war, the younger brother"], [741.65, 743.7, "Atahualpa won"], [744.166, 746.566, "But the empire he took"], [746.733, 748.616, "was no longer the old Inca"], [748.933, 750.65, "Half lost to disease"], [750.733, 752.766, "a nation torn apart by civil war"], [752.85, 755.05, "The conquered tribes were secretly"], [755.216, 756.533, "sharpening their knives"], [756.833, 758.133, "Drunk on victory"], [758.25, 759.866, "Atahualpa did not know"], [760.083, 762.533, "that at that very moment, strangers"], [762.816, 764.133, "had just landed on the coast"], [764.9, 766.633, "Those who landed were the Spanish"], [767.6, 769.55, "Their commander: Francisco Pizarro"], [770.6, 773.1, "The size of his army: just 168 men"], [774.066, 775.4, "and 27 horses"], [777.283, 779.65, "168 men against an empire of 10 million"], [779.733, 781.533, "By the numbers, it was madness"], [784.25, 785.2, "Pizarro asked to meet"], [785.266, 787.4, "the emperor Atahualpa"], [788.633, 790.666, "Atahualpa scoffed"], [791.766, 792.883, "Just 168 men"], [793.0, 794.533, "what was there to fear?"], [795.433, 795.833, "He went"], [795.833, 797.15, "to the plaza of a city"], [797.233, 797.833, "called Cajamarca"], [797.833, 799.666, "leading thousands of people"], [800.55, 802.516, "But he did not go to fight"], [803.466, 804.816, "just to meet his visitors"], [805.4, 807.233, "Most of them carried no weapons"], [808.1, 809.516, "The moment the emperor"], [809.6